# agentic-sf environment, for a factory stamped with `--harness claude_code`.
#
# THERE IS NO API KEY TO SET for this harness: the Claude Code CLI brings its
# own auth (`claude auth`). An agent you move to `harness: pi` needs that
# provider's key here, e.g. OPENROUTER_API_KEY.

# Where the agentic-sf skill itself lives. install.py fills this in from the
# path it ran from and leaves whatever is already here alone.
ASF_SKILL=

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_PATH=claude               # Claude Code binary if not on PATH
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name

# ── the cockpit: LOCAL or TEAM ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# install.py asks which (`--cockpit local|team`); this file is where the answer
# lives, and you may change it here at any time.
#
# LOCAL — the default: ASF_COCKPIT_URL unset. `asf up` starts a cockpit on this
# machine — the same images a team deploys, on Docker, at http://localhost:3000
# — issues itself a token and ships every session to it. Only you see it.
#
# TEAM — a shared cockpit: everyone's sessions in one place, and claims, so two
# stations never start the same work item. Two values, both from whoever runs it:
#
#   ASF_COCKPIT_URL    the backend's SITE origin, where stations ship. Not the
#                      cockpit's page (:3000) and not its API (:3210):
#                        docker compose  its CONVEX_SITE_ORIGIN, e.g. https://cockpit.example.com:3211
#                        Convex Cloud    https://<deployment>.convex.site
#   ASF_COCKPIT_TOKEN  an INGEST token for THIS repository, issued by the
#                      cockpit's operator with the deployment's admin access
#                      and printed once. It adds this factory's events and reads
#                      nothing back. Name the factory as its repository,
#                      owner/name — a team cockpit shows a session only to
#                      people the forge lets read that repository:
#                        docker compose  docker compose exec app ./convex.sh run tokens:issue '{"factory": "acme/widgets"}'
#                        Convex Cloud    npx convex run tokens:issue '{"factory": "acme/widgets"}'   (in apps/cockpit; --prod for production)
#
# Then `just station-sync` ships what this checkout has (it fails only when the
# token is refused), and `just station-register` lets the cockpit send this
# checkout commands — a person with write access approves the code it prints.
# A CI job names the same two values: vars.ASF_COCKPIT_URL, secrets.ASF_COCKPIT_TOKEN.
# ASF_COCKPIT_URL=https://cockpit.example.com:3211
# ASF_COCKPIT_TOKEN=asf_ingest_…
# ASF_STATION_NAME=                # how the cockpit names this checkout; default <login>@<host>:<dir>

# The LOCAL cockpit's knobs (ignored with ASF_COCKPIT_URL set). The version is
# never older than asf/cockpit/min-version; name a newer release to run that
# one. It asks the forge as you: `asf up` hands it what `gh auth token` prints,
# for GH_HOST when that is set (an Enterprise Server) and github.com otherwise.
# Nothing to set here — the token is never written to this file.
# ASF_COCKPIT_VERSION=
# ASF_COCKPIT_APP_PORT=3000
# ASF_COCKPIT_BACKEND_PORT=3210
# ASF_COCKPIT_SITE_PORT=3211
# How many days the local cockpit keeps a finished session's transcript before
# aging it out (factory.yaml's cockpit.transcript_retention_days can only
# shorten it). Raise it here if you want them longer.
# ASF_COCKPIT_TRANSCRIPT_DAYS=30
